<<<
to describe as ‘a somewhat amazing fascination °. Thus:—The evidence furnished in the somewhat extraordinary report of the Federation as to its waste of huge sums of money on . . ./His election experiences were somewhat wnique./ The flocks of wild geese, to which the flamingo is somewhat more or less closely allied. / The Labour motion introduced the proviso, somewhat for the first time, that the process should be gradual.
===
to describe as ‘a somewhat amazing fascination’. Thus:—*The evidence furnished in the somewhat extraordinary report of the Federation as to its waste of huge sums of money on . . ./His election experiences were somewhat unique./The flocks of wild geese, to which the flamingo is somewhat more or less closely allied./The Labour motion introduced the proviso, somewhat for the first time, that the process should be gradual.*
>>>
